rop=none","line":97,"embedded":true},{"title":"Why We Get Fat","target":"http://www.nytimes.com/2010/12/28/health/28zuger.html?_r=0","line":123},{"title":"Zoë Harcombe","target":"http://www.zoeharcombe.com/","line":135},{"title":"that dietary saturated fat is associated","target":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC2824152/","line":139},{"title":"Illustration by Pete Gamlen","target":"https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/23933cc2b353092de836a189213581a83d4f2fbe/109_434_2733_4178/master/2733.jpg?width=445&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none","line":145,"embedded":true},{"title":"Always Hungry, David Ludwig","target":"http://drdavidludwig.com/","line":155},{"title":"Robert Atkins","target":"https://www.theguardian.com/news/2003/apr/19/guardianobituaries.williamleith","line":163},{"title":"high-fat, low-carbohydrate diet","target":"https://www.theguardian.com/uk/2003/sep/21/society.politics","line":163},{"title":"in a trial","target":"http://annals.org/article.aspx?articleid=1900694","line":171},{"title":"Illustration by Pete Gamlen","target":"https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/c87f8e7fe993adf5ed4f4a30831c83bbea018f6d/0_0_2928_4763/master/2928.jpg?width=445&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none","line":173,"embedded":true},{"title":"told the Washington Post","target":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/wonk/wp/2015/12/18/congress-we-need-to-review-the-dietary-guidelines-for-americans/","line":181},{"title":"wrote an article for the BMJ","target":"http://www.bmj.com/content/351/bmj.h4962","line":185},{"title":"Food","target":"https://www.theguardian.com/food","line":195},{"title":"@mrianleslie","target":"https://twitter.com/mrianleslie","line":211}],"metadata":{"title":"The sugar conspiracy | Ian Leslie","source":"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2016/apr/07/the-sugar-conspiracy-robert-lustig-john-yudkin","author":["[[the Guardian]]"],"published":"2016-04-07","created":"2025-04-28","description":"<strong>The Long Read:</strong> In 1972, a British scientist sounded the alarm that sugar – and not fat – was the greatest danger to our health. But his findings were ridiculed and his reputation ruined. How did the world’s top nutrition scientists get it so wrong for so long?","tags":[]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"fswd8i","at":1778088458110},"key":"Clippings/The sugar conspiracy  Ian Leslie.md"},
